                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I had really low expectations for this game and somehow it managed to suck even more than I could have possibly imagined. All I wanted was to take a few swings at balls and aim for homeruns in a quirky VR baseball game. \n\nThe problem is that it does not play like proper baseball and I don't say this because it's an arcade game in nature. I wasn't looking for a very realistic simulation but the basic element of hitting the balls feels completely wrong. Forget about holding a virtual bat two handed like a proper baseball player. The best way to play this game is to hold the bat one handed and go for swings like you are holding a tennis or badminton racket. The strength of your swings barely matters too. The best ''bat'' to use is actually ping pong racket (needs to be unlocked first), that says a lot about the gameplay. Clearly this is not what I expected out of a game called VR Slugger.\n\nI cannot recommend this game for people looking for a good baseball experience in VR. If you're looking for a collection of tennis mini-games masquerading as a baseball game then this game is for you... but that's quite a niche and even then the game isn't worth the asking price due to the low amount of content. \n\nFinal score: 4/10",
